    "scope": "Production segmented configuration forwards admitted slot grants; native geometry, request/process admission, bridge resizing and existing load/SSD/allocator/factory/telemetry/benchmark regressions. Deletes legacy eager-pool provider capacity policy.",
    "limits": [
      "Synthetic fleet envelopes use exact native dtype/model geometry and deliberately synthetic resident weights/OS snapshots; these do not establish model fit or measured capacity on 36/64/128 GiB hardware.",
      "Manual loops inside test functions are not counted as separate framework cases.",
      "No requested full-size model, normal HTTP, release default or performance validation in this gate.",
      "Historical co-residency live test changes compile but its model-gated execution is not included.",
      "Pre-evaluation real-native cap is temporarily constrained at observation boundary then restored before allocation; not continuously bounded whole-model/factory/scratch proof.",
      "Real allocator test OS availability is non-binding; coherent actual allocator usage is retained.",
      "Shared SSD and real allocator suites use separate processes.",
      "Opt-in production-grant benchmark mode and final requested-model runs remain mandatory.",
      "Existing GPT factory test corrected to full admitted segmented grant and empty backing, plus constructor comment. Full factory97 rerun on candidate2. Other14 groups executed on candidate1 with unchanged production/dependency/test bytes; carried evidence is not candidate2 invocation."
    ],
